<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!--
  The success page shares the checkout's stylesheet.

  components/_checkout.less carries the .checkout-onepage-success rules
  alongside the step rules, so this handle enqueues the same file rather than
  splitting a third bundle out for one page. See web/css/spartrak-checkout.less.
-->
<page xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
      xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="urn:magento:framework:View/Layout/etc/page_configuration.xsd">
    <head>
        <css src="css/spartrak-checkout.css"/>
    </head>
    <body>
        <!--
          ===================================================================
          POINTING THE BLOCK BACK AT THE TEMPLATE THIS THEME ACTUALLY OVERRIDES
          ===================================================================
          The theme's Magento_Checkout/templates/success.phtml was never being
          rendered. Not a fallback problem, not a cache problem — the file was
          byte-identical on the server, the theme resolved every other template
          on the page, and a full cache:flush changed nothing.

          Magento's own in-store-pickup module REPOINTS the block:

              vendor/magento/module-inventory-in-store-pickup-frontend
                  /view/frontend/layout/checkout_onepage_success.xml
              <referenceBlock name="checkout.success"
                              template="Magento_InventoryInStorePickupFrontend::success.phtml">

          So `checkout.success` stopped asking for Magento_Checkout::success.phtml
          altogether, and overriding that path could never take effect. Confirmed
          with template path hints on the live success page, which named
          .../module-inventory-in-store-pickup-frontend/.../success.phtml as the
          file that produced "Your order number is: …".

          This storefront does not use Magento's in-store pickup — collection
          from a branch or depot is Spartrak_PickupLocation, a separate
          implementation — so that template has nothing to contribute here and
          Figma 554:12434 defines the page.

          IT IS SET HERE, IN THE THEME, RATHER THAN IN Spartrak_Checkout, because
          theme layout is merged after every module's. Fixing it module-side
          would mean adding Magento_InventoryInStorePickupFrontend to that
          module's <sequence> purely to win a merge order, which couples this
          module to one that may be disabled. The theme always wins, and the
          choice of template is presentation — the theme's own concern.

          Only the template attribute is stated: layout merging is a deep merge,
          so Spartrak_Checkout's `success_view_model` argument on this same block
          survives untouched, which is what the template needs to render.
        -->
        <referenceBlock name="checkout.success" template="Magento_Checkout::success.phtml"/>
    </body>
</page>
